  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Fluffy** (1 review): Deaner plays with fierce intensity on Fluffy [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Stallion 3**: rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **I'll Be Your Johnny on the Spot**: back after 54 archived shows (511 days) [4]\n- **Sweet Texas Fire**: back after 58 archived shows (582 days) [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Argus [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2003-09-12.akg483.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 152 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording's sound quality is good [3]\n- **09-track-09_20200827_1715**: source not stated; 29 songs; 149 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taper dedicated the recording to Johnny Cash, who died that day [1]\n- Reviewer calls it their favorite Asheville show and favorite Ween show overall [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2003-09-12.akg483.flac16**: taped by Gordon Wilson; transferred by Cliff Lawless; source: AKG 480/ck63 (XY 90) > Apogee AD1000 (@ 48kHz) > Tascam DAP1 [1]. Also: Transferred via Sony TCD-D8 to Wavelab 4.0c, resampled to 44.1kHz, then tracked and FLAC encoded at level 5 in CD Wave [1]",
